{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Auto-exposure convergence gate with the SCREEN-SPACE passes live",
    "(spec 10.2 phase 4). Run with --ssgi --fog.",
    "",
    "10.1 demonstrated convergence on a bare punctual-lit room, where SSR",
    "contributed nothing (no catcher-marked surface), and SSGI and fog were off.",
    "So it proved the loop stable on the one configuration in which none of the",
    "clamps that meter through it were live -- WS_REFLECT_MAX, WS_BOUNCE_MAX and",
    "WS_MEDIA_MAX all sit upstream of the metering pass.",
    "",
    "Sky mode rather than an HDR file so the fixture needs nothing outside the",
    "repo; the catcher (and therefore SSR) requires an IBL to exist at all.",
    "Auto-exposure is left ON -- that is the whole point, so no exposure key."
  ],
  "models": [
    { "path": "sss_fixture.gltf" }
  ],
  "environment": {
    "mode": "sky",
    "sun": { "elevation": 22.0, "azimuth": 130.0 }
  },
  "camera": {
    "eye": [0.0, 0.35, 1.6],
    "target": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0],
    "fov": 40
  },
  "post": {
    "tonemap": "neutral",
    "auto_exposure": true,
    "fog": {
      "enabled": true,
      "density": 0.08,
      "near": 0.0,
      "far": 60.0,
      "depthDistribution": 1.0
    }
  }
}
